# FileShare — Product Requirements Document (PRD)

## 1. Vision

**FileShare** is a browser-based, peer-to-peer file sharing tool powered by WebRTC. Files transfer directly between devices — no cloud, no accounts, no uploads to third-party servers. The goal is to become the fastest, simplest way to send a file to someone nearby.

---

## 2. Current State (Prototype Analysis)

Your existing prototype at [server.js](file:///d:/coding/FileShare/server.js) and [index.html](file:///d:/coding/FileShare/public/index.html) already implements a functional P2P file transfer system:

| Feature | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Socket.io signaling server | ✅ Working | Room-code based discovery |
| WebRTC peer connection | ✅ Working | STUN servers configured |
| File chunking (64KB) | ✅ Working | Adaptive buffer management |
| Speed meter (MB/s) | ✅ Working | 1-second interval |
| Transfer progress (%) | ✅ Working | Throttled UI updates |
| Auto-download on completion | ✅ Working | Blob reassembly + download link |
| Image preview | ✅ Working | For image MIME types |
| Buffered send with backpressure | ✅ Working | HIGH_WATER / LOW_WATER thresholds |

### Known Gaps (from risk analysis & code review)

| Gap | Severity |
|---|---|
| No TURN server → fails behind strict NATs/firewalls | 🔴 High |
| No encryption layer beyond DTLS (no E2E application-level encryption) | 🟡 Medium |
| No multi-file / folder support | 🟡 Medium |
| No drag-and-drop UX | 🟡 Medium |
| Raw prototype UI — not production-ready | 🟡 Medium |
| No mobile responsiveness | 🟡 Medium |
| No transfer resume on disconnect | 🟡 Medium |
| No QR code for room sharing | 🟢 Low |
| No PWA / installability | 🟢 Low |
| Room codes are manually entered (no auto-discovery) | 🟢 Low |

---

## 3. Competitive Landscape Research

### 3.1 Open-Source Web Apps (Direct Competitors)

| Project | Tech | Key Differentiators | Weakness |
|---|---|---|---|
| **[PairDrop](https://github.com/nickvdhoudt/pairdrop)** | Node.js, Vanilla JS, WebRTC, WebSockets | Auto-discovery on LAN, persistent device pairing via QR/6-digit code, temporary public rooms (5-letter code), PWA, text/clipboard sharing, ZIP multi-file, TURN relay | Complex codebase, harder to self-host without Docker |
| **[FilePizza](https://github.com/kern/filepizza)** | Node.js, React, WebRTC | Password-protected shares, shareable URL links, multi-file ZIP, dark mode, Redis-backed state | Sender must keep tab open, no LAN auto-discovery |
| **[Instant.io](https://github.com/webtorrent/instant.io)** | WebTorrent (BitTorrent+WebRTC) | Magnet link sharing, streaming video/audio in browser, multi-peer swarm | Only works with WebTorrent-compatible clients, no direct peer targeting |

### 3.2 Native Apps (Broader Ecosystem)

| Project | Tech | Key Differentiators |
|---|---|---|
| **[LocalSend](https://github.com/localsend/localsend)** | Flutter, REST API, UDP multicast | Cross-platform native app (Win/Mac/Linux/iOS/Android), mDNS/multicast discovery, HTTPS with self-signed TLS, no internet needed, "reverse file transfer" browser mode |
| **[KDE Connect](https://kdeconnect.kde.org/)** | C++/Qt | Phone↔Desktop integration suite (clipboard, notifications, remote control + file transfer) |
| **[Syncthing](https://syncthing.net/)** | Go | Continuous folder sync, not one-off transfers |

### 3.3 CLI Tools (Command-Line P2P Transfer)

| Tool | Language | Key Features |
|---|---|---|
| **[croc](https://github.com/schollz/croc)** | Go | Single binary, PAKE encryption, transfer resume, folder support, cross-platform |
| **[magic-wormhole](https://github.com/magic-wormhole/magic-wormhole)** | Python | Well-audited SPAKE2 protocol, classic UX (`wormhole send/receive`) |
| **[Wormhole-William](https://github.com/psanford/wormhole-william)** | Go | Go rewrite of magic-wormhole, single binary |
| **[fs-cli](https://github.com/)** | Go | WebRTC data channels specifically, concurrent file transfers |

### 3.4 Libraries You Can Build With

| Library | Type | Best For |
|---|---|---|
| **[PeerJS](https://peerjs.com/)** | JS (Browser) | Batteries-included WebRTC — includes a free signaling server + simple `conn.send()` API |
| **[simple-peer](https://github.com/feross/simple-peer)** | JS (Browser + Node) | Low-level WebRTC wrapper, great flexibility, used by WebTorrent |
| **[simple-peer-files](https://github.com/nickvdhoudt/simple-peer-files)** | JS (Browser) | Adds pause/resume to simple-peer file transfers |
| **[node-datachannel](https://github.com/nicolvdhoudt/node-datachannel)** | Node.js | Native C++ bindings for high-perf server-side WebRTC data channels |
| **[aiortc](https://github.com/aiortc/aiortc)** | Python | Full WebRTC/ORTC in Python (asyncio), great for non-browser peers |
| **[peerjs-python](https://github.com/ambianic/peerjs-python)** | Python | Python ↔ PeerJS browser client interop |
| **[WebTorrent](https://github.com/nickvdhoudt/webtorrent)** | JS | BitTorrent protocol over WebRTC, multi-peer swarm |
| **[zip.js](https://gildas-lormeau.github.io/zip.js/)** | JS (Browser) | Client-side ZIP compression for multi-file bundles |

### 3.5 MCP (Model Context Protocol) Servers

MCP for WebRTC file sharing is an **emerging pattern** where:
- The MCP server exposes tools like `create-room`, `join-room`, `send-file` 
- AI agents can orchestrate P2P file transfers programmatically
- Actual data flows over WebRTC (never through the MCP server)

> [!NOTE]
> No mature, production-ready MCP server for file sharing exists yet. This is a greenfield opportunity if you want to differentiate FileShare down the road.

